In computer programming, a code smell is any characteristic in the source code of a program that possibly indicates a deeper problem.
Now I will tell you the definition about SonarQube warning 'S1659':'Multiple variables should not be declared on the same line' as given by the SonarQube docu, including an example to help you solve a similar warning:
'Declaring multiple variables on one line is difficult to read.

Noncompliant Code Example


    class MyClass {

      private int a, b;

      public void method(){
        int c; int d;
      }
    }


Compliant Solution


    class MyClass {

      private int a;
      private int b;

      public void method(){
        int c;
        int d;
      }
    }


